Discovery: SDD

Purpose:
  Project Discovery and Reverse-Engineering Engine. Enables AI to
  understand existing (brownfield) projects by analyzing source code
  and inferring architecture, stack, domains, tests, security,
  infrastructure, and documentation. Discovery NEVER modifies
  source code — it only observes, infers, validates, and models.

Owns: ./

Modes:
  GREENFIELD — new project from business input
  BROWNFIELD — existing project from source code
  HYBRID — existing project with new requirements

Rules:
  [DSC1]  Discovery MUST analyze, not modify source code.
  [DSC2]  Discovery results MUST be classified as FACT, INFERRED,
          UNKNOWN, or CONFLICT.
  [DSC3]  Confidence level MUST accompany every inference.
  [DSC4]  Discovery MUST NOT overwrite .sdd without human/agent decision.
  [DSC5]  Discovery MUST detect drift between .sdd and source.
  [DSC6]  Discovery MUST produce actionable backlog, not just report.
  [DSC7]  Discovery MUST respect "Analyze ? Modify" principle.
  [DSC8]  Discovery baseline MUST be created for future comparison.
  [DSC9]  Discovery MUST detect circular dependencies.
  [DSC10] Discovery MUST identify security gaps.
  [DR1]   Discovery MUST analyze, not modify source code.
  [DR2]   Discovery MUST classify all findings.
  [DR3]   Discovery MUST assign confidence to inferences.
  [DR4]   Discovery MUST detect drift between .sdd and source.
  [DR5]   Discovery MUST produce actionable backlog.
  [DR6]   Discovery MUST create baseline for future comparison.
  [DR7]   Discovery MUST detect circular dependencies.
  [DR8]   Discovery MUST identify security gaps.
  [CF1]   Every inference MUST have confidence level.
  [CF2]   HIGH confidence findings MAY be treated as FACT.
  [CF3]   MEDIUM confidence findings MUST be validated for critical decisions.
  [CF4]   LOW confidence findings MUST be marked UNKNOWN if critical.
  [CF5]   Confidence MUST NOT be inflated for convenience.
  [BL1]   Baseline MUST be created after every discovery.
  [BL2]   Baseline MUST be immutable after creation.
  [BL3]   Future discoveries MUST compare against baseline.
  [BL4]   Baseline MUST include discovery score and unknown budget.

FactClassification:
  FACT: Directly proven from source code
  INFERRED: Logical conclusion from source code
  UNKNOWN: No information available
  CONFLICT: .sdd differs from source

ConfidenceLevels:
  HIGH:
    Definition: Directly proven from source
    Evidence: Multiple indicators, explicit configuration
    Action: Treat as FACT
  MEDIUM:
    Definition: Strong inference from source
    Evidence: Clear patterns, consistent usage
    Action: Treat as INFERRED, validate if critical
  LOW:
    Definition: Weak inference
    Evidence: Single indicator, ambiguous
    Action: Treat as INFERRED, mark as UNKNOWN if critical

Baseline:
  Structure: Project, Mode, Timestamp
  Scores: Overall, Structure, Stack, Architecture, Testing, Security, Infrastructure, Documentation
  UnknownBudget: Unknown percentage
  Sections: Discovered lists, Conflicts, Gaps, ActionableBacklog
  Rules: immutable after creation, compare future discoveries against it

ReadOrder:
   1  @scanners.sdd
   2  @detectors.sdd
   3  @conflicts.sdd
   4  @gitignore-integration.sdd

Navigation:
  Discovery: @discovery/INDEX.sdd
  Scanners: @discovery/scanners.sdd
  Detectors: @discovery/detectors.sdd
  Conflicts: @discovery/conflicts.sdd
  GitignoreIntegration: @discovery/gitignore-integration.sdd
  ProjectMode: @project/mode.sdd

State: +
